Verse 1:
[Ab]I've found a Friend; oh, [Eb7]such a Friend! He loved me ere I [Ab]knew Him;
He drew me with the [Db]cords of love, And [Ab]thus He [Eb7]bound me to [Ab]Him.
And '[Eb7]round my heart still [Ab]closely twine Those [Db]ties which [Bb]nought can [Ab]se[Eb]ver,
[Eb7]For [Ab]I am His, and [Db]He is mine, For[Ab]ever [Eb7]and forev[Ab]er.

Verse 2:
[Ab]I've found [Eb7]a Friend; oh, [Ab]such a Friend!
[Db]He [Ab]bled, He [Eb7]died to [Ab]save me;
[Eb7]And [Ab]not [Db]alone [Bb]the [Ab]gift [Eb]of life,
[Eb7]But [Ab]His [Db]own [Ab]self [Eb7]He [Ab]gave me.
